B.bvn=new A.k("Use tone 30 instead of 10 for onColors on containers in LIGHT mode. This is a new Material-3 spec standard. It is more color expressive, but reduces contrast.\n\nThis modifier ONLY impacts LIGHT scheme variants where the container on colors use tone 10. For scheme variants with an intentionally custom tone for onColors on containers, this setting has no impact. Such variants are:\n - Fidelity\n - Monochrome\n - Content\n - Ultra Contrast\n - Candy pop\n - Chroma\n\nThis feature is not yet used by Flutter's ColorScheme.fromSeed produced ColorSchemes, but will be when Flutter upgrades to Material Color Utilities (MCU) 0.12.0. You can opt in on using it already now, or decide not to use it. With FSS you will be able to do so, even after it becomes a forced default and the only option in Flutter's ColorScheme.fromSeed.\n\nFor MCU seed generated schemes, this only has any impact when contrast level is at the default value (0), normal contrast.\n\nWhen using FFS seed generated schemes, the tones modifier \"B&W main onColors\" will override this setting.\n",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
