B.bx6=new A.k("Hover, focus, highlight, pressed and splash colors get a slight primary color tint, or tint of its own color, if it is not primary colored.\n\nKeep OFF for Flutter's mostly grey defaults. Turn it ON for subtly more color expressive interaction styles. We like it and recommend it. It also makes interactions more consistent. By default Material-3 uses tinted interactions on some newer components, but it is not applied to all components. This settings also remedies this gap where it is possible.\n\nThe ON state impacts ThemeData hover, focus, highlight and splash colors. Material-3 components implement their own interaction effects via WidgetState color properties. This also styles all Material components on component theme level. Most components are covered, a few cases may not be fully supported due to lack of support or issues in the Flutter framework. Their later inclusion in this setting will be reported as new features, not as style breaking.\n",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
